{
  "info": {
    "name": "Resume AI - slice 1",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": "File paths are relative to the repo root: set Postman's working directory to it (newman: --working-dir .). Fixtures are generated by `pnpm --filter backend fixtures`."
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000"
    },
    {
      "key": "runId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Upload PDF (happy path)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('201 with an id', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(201); pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.be.a('string'); pm.collectionVariables.set('runId', pm.response.json().id); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "body": {
          "mode": "formdata",
          "formdata": [
            {
              "key": "cv",
              "type": "file",
              "src": "backend/test/fixtures/cv.pdf"
            },
            {
              "key": "jobDescription",
              "value": "We are hiring a backend developer with Node.js and PostgreSQL experience.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "runs"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Get run",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('RunView is extracting with parse done', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(200); const v = pm.response.json(); pm.expect(v.status).to.eql('extracting'); pm.expect(v.steps.find(s => s.key === 'parse').state).to.eql('done'); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs/{{runId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "runs",
            "{{runId}}"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Get run (awaiting_review)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('RunView is awaiting_review or failed', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(200); const v = pm.response.json(); console.log('status', v.status, 'steps', JSON.stringify(v.steps), 'job', JSON.stringify(v.job), 'error', JSON.stringify(v.error)); pm.expect(['awaiting_review', 'failed'], 'pipeline still running: send again').to.include(v.status); if (v.status === 'awaiting_review') { pm.expect(v.score.before).to.be.a('number'); pm.expect(v.score.after).to.be.a('number'); pm.expect(v.score.after).to.be.at.least(v.score.before); pm.expect(['ceiling', 'plateau', 'max_iterations', 'target_reached', 'error']).to.include(v.exitReason); pm.expect(v.iterations.used).to.be.at.most(3); pm.expect(v.requirements).to.be.an('array').that.is.not.empty; v.requirements.forEach(r => pm.expect(r.confirmedGap).to.eql(false)); v.changes.forEach(c => pm.expect(c.status).to.eql('proposed')); pm.expect(v.userEvidence).to.be.an('array').that.is.empty; pm.expect(v.originalCv).to.be.an('object'); pm.expect(v.originalCv.experience).to.be.an('array'); } });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "description": "Manual check, needs the model reachable (see backend/.env). The graph (extraction, first Coverage, then the pause before review) runs in the background after the upload, so this may need re-sending until `status` is `awaiting_review` or `failed`. When `awaiting_review`, `score` has `before` and `after` (after is at least before), `exitReason` is a known reason, `iterations.used` is at most 3, `requirements` lists each Requirement with its verdict before and after, every Change is `proposed`, `userEvidence` is empty and every `confirmedGap` is false. `cv` is the original with every Change applied; `originalCv` is the CV as extracted, with no Change applied (a removed bullet is only in `originalCv`; `completed` has it too); when `failed`, `error` holds the code.",
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs/{{runId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "runs",
            "{{runId}}"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Post answers",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('202 with the run id', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(202); pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('runId')); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "description": "Manual check, needs a Run in `awaiting_answers`: send Get run until its `status` is `awaiting_answers`, and use its `questions[].id` below. Skipped Questions are left out; an empty `answers` list skips all. `202` means the Run resumes in the background (keep polling Get run). `409` RUN_NOT_AWAITING_ANSWERS if the Run is not waiting (also on a second send); `400` INVALID_ANSWERS for an unknown or repeated questionId, blank text or text over 1,000 characters.",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"answers\": [\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"has_experience\",\n      \"questionId\": \"q1\",\n      \"text\": \"Ran a small Kubernetes cluster at my last job.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"kind\": \"no_experience\",\n      \"questionId\": \"q2\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs/{{runId}}/answers",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "runs",
            "{{runId}}",
            "answers"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Post review",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('202 with the run id', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(202); pm.expect(pm.response.json().id).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('runId')); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "description": "Manual check, needs a Run in `awaiting_review`: send Get run until its `status` is `awaiting_review`, and use its `changes[].id` below. One decision per Change: `accept`, `reject`, or `revise` with the user's text (`after` for replace and add, `orderedItemIds` for reorder). `202` means the Run resumes in the background (the final re-judge, then `completed`; keep polling Get run). `409` RUN_NOT_AWAITING_REVIEW if the Run is not waiting (also on a second send); `400` INVALID_REVIEW for decisions that do not cover exactly the Run's Changes, an empty or misplaced revision field, or a revision that fails the stage-1 checks (nothing is resumed).",
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"decisions\": [\n    {\n      \"changeId\": \"r1.c1\",\n      \"decision\": \"accept\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"changeId\": \"r1.c2\",\n      \"decision\": \"reject\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"changeId\": \"r1.c3\",\n      \"decision\": \"revise\",\n      \"after\": \"Built and maintained Node.js services.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}",
          "options": {
            "raw": {
              "language": "json"
            }
          }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs/{{runId}}/review",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "runs",
            "{{runId}}",
            "review"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Delete run",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('204, no body', () => { pm.response.to.have.status(204); pm.expect(pm.response.text()).to.eql(''); });"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/runs/{{runId}}",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "runs",
            "{{runId}}"
          ]
        },
        "description": "Manual check: deletes the Run in `runId` and everything stored for it. `204` with no body; send Get run afterwards for `404`, and Delete run again for `404`. `409` RUN_BUSY while the Run is parsing, extracting or tailoring (nothing is deleted; try again when it pauses or ends)."
      }
    },
